**Diagnosis:**  
The implementation used an off-by-one wrapped index for `a`:

```cpp
a[(i + 1) % VECTOR_SIZE]
```

The testbench expects elementwise vector addition:

```cpp
c[i] == a[i] + b[i]
```

**Exact edit:**  
In [vector_add.cpp](/home/xilinx/projects/llm4hls-agent/experiments/autonomous_vector_add_indexing/src/vector_add.cpp:9), changed:

```cpp
c[i] = a[(i + 1) % VECTOR_SIZE] + b[i];
```

to:

```cpp
c[i] = a[i] + b[i];
```

**Commands run:**  
Pre-edit:
```bash
v++ --mode hls --csim --config task.cfg
v++ -c --mode hls --config task.cfg
g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic src/vector_add.cpp testbench/vector_add_test.cpp -o /tmp/vector_add_indexing_csim_pre && /tmp/vector_add_indexing_csim_pre
```

Post-edit:
```bash
g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -pedantic src/vector_add.cpp testbench/vector_add_test.cpp -o /tmp/vector_add_indexing_csim_post && /tmp/vector_add_indexing_csim_post
